      "message": "selftest: Remove module and test built-in SHA256 directly\n\nAfter moving the SHA256 check into the hash module, selftest.h only had\na one-line wrapper left. Drop it and call secp256k1_sha256_selftest\nfrom secp256k1_selftest directly, with a comment explaining why it\nalways uses the built-in implementation: the API function is meant to\ncatch a broken build of the library (e.g., wrong endianness), and a\ncompression override is already checked when it is set on a context.",
